WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.940
The Digital World,

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.100
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.490
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.280
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.990
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.750
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:56.380
DarkKnightmon used the Dark Stone 
to resurrect all the Death Generals,

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.200
then stole my Digimon's souls 
and sent them to Prison Land.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:05.260
To get their souls back,

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:09.170
I let DarkKnightmon take my soul 
and send me to Prison Land, too.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.790
But the seven Death 
Generals awaited me there.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:24.410
<b>For the Future of the Digital World!</b>

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:24.410
<b>Friendship with the Death Generals!</b>

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.240
For the Future of the Digital World!

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.320
Friendship with the Death Generals!

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.630
Here we go, everyone!

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.840
Shoutmon!

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.350
Okay!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.810
Ballistamon!

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.140
Dorulumon!

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.520
DigiXros!

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:22.260
Shoutmon X3!

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.520
And what can the likes of X3 accomplish?

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.590
Take this!

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.420
Dragon Breath Tonic Fire!

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.730
Three Victorize!

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.500
Too easy.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.870
No, wait.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.210
Not bad, for a measly X3.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.550
I told you,

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.680
in a contest of burning 
hearts, we won't lose!

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.780
Well, who's next?

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.050
Interesting.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.890
How long can you keep up such big talk?

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.090
Nightmare Raid!

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.030
Hydro Pressure!

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:16.970
Time to finish you!

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.820
The World Shot!

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.710
X3!

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.150
Taiki Kudou,

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:32.260
you came here to take back their souls,

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:36.920
but if their souls are lost here, 
their lives are lost, as well.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.330
Apollomon, I'm going to 
take your soul back, too.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.100
Foolishness.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.430
Apollomon's just heart 
does not exist here.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:51.870
This body is under the complete control 
of the evil dark spot, Whispered.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.080
Why?

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.770
Whispered should have been 
completely destroyed!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:00.620
The seven generals were resurrected 
by the power of the Dark Stone.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.580
Naturally, Apollomon's soul 
is now part of the evil me.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.000
No way!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.900
Apollomon's just heart 
would never lose to you!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.620
Then I'll convince you by crushing you.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.720
Get him, Olegmon.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.780
Huh? Me?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:18.850
Olegmon...

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.110
Taiki, you and I are enemies, after all.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.940
It's our destiny to fight.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:27.100
Are you really okay with that?

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:27.770
What?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.610
Are you, someone who 
treasures his friends,

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:34.250
okay with fighting under someone 
who doesn't value friendship?

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.610
What do you mean?

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:40.180
DarkKnightmon only 
resurrected your bodies

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.720
because he doesn't trust any of you!

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:48.430
Olegmon, I believe in your heart 
because it truly values friendship!

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:52.300
And I believe that, deep inside, 
you have a just heart that hates evil!

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.290
Olegmon, don't be fooled by the enemy.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.900
I know!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:04.210
<i>True, I don't appreciate 
that DarkKnightmon is</i>

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.270
<i>using us as he pleases when I 
thought he'd been destroyed.</i>

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:10.050
<i>But this boy alone is 
the one I just can't...</i>

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.880
<i>What was that?</i>

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.890
<i>No, it couldn't be.</i>

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.430
If Olegmon won't do it, I will.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:23.430
Stop!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.730
Taiki Kudou...

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:28.110
you would become a shield 
for your friends?

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:31.100
You do very strange things, as always.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.460
You wouldn't understand,

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:36.170
since you don't have any real friends!

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.130
Friends...

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:41.780
Taiki!

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.850
All talk and no substance.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.390
Gravimon, stop dragging it 
out and finish him, now.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.260
What?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.030
Just a minute, Apollomon Whispered.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.910
When did you become our leader?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:02.500
That's right. We don't have 
to take orders from you.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.100
It's obvious that the 
strongest takes the lead.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.150
I can't overlook that.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.210
We'll take you on here and now.

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.190
Wait a minute, you guys!

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:14.120
Is this any time for 
fighting among friends?

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:15.510
Friends?

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.250
We are not friends.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.920
We're just not enemies.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.520
What?

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.580
What are you all doing here?

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.260
I'm in the middle of a 
wager with Taiki Kudou.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:36.500
We know. We'll be waiting 
here with you for Taiki.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.900
I see.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:40.770
However, waiting may be a waste of time.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.820
Taiki and the others will come back!

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:44.280
Yeah!

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.610
I hope so.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.920
That would give the Death Generals 
a more worthwhile fight.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.320
<i>Taiki, what's taking you so long?</i>

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:00.360
Taiki!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.530
How long can you hold out?

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:05.860
D-Darn it...

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.640
Stay down, Taiki!

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:08.860
If this keeps up...

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.470
Taiki's life is in danger!

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.870
All right, I will finish him off.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.280
Bloody Stream Glade!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:20.950
Taiki!

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:25.800
<i>Are you okay with fighting under 
someone who doesn't value friendship?</i>

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.790
<i>We are not friends.</i>

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:30.760
<i>We're just not enemies.</i>

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:35.140
<i>Olegmon, I believe in your heart 
because it truly values friendship!</i>

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:41.900
What?!

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.580
Why, you... Are you betraying me?

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.370
You better believe it!

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.740
I like guys who treasure their friends!

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.410
He's...

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:54.640
Thank you, Olegmon!

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.560
No need to thank me.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.620
This suited me better 
from the start, anyway.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.520
You've got guts.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.620
Then I only have to annihilate 
you along with them.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.390
Arrow of Whispered!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:10.970
Olegmon!

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.730
This is nothing!

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.370
What are you all doing?

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:19.260
Attack him!

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.170
I don't think so.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.440
We won't accept your orders.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.480
Let's see what you can do.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.680
Very well.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.320
Olegmon!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.200
Destroying the traitor comes 
before destroying Taiki Kudou!

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.180
Shoutmon!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.260
I won't forgive you!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.030
We'll fight, too!

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.130
This is no time to be lying around!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.300
That's right!

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.870
Our new friend is trying his hardest!

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:53.170
Hey, you're gonna make me blush.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.670
They still have the strength to stand?

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.220
This is a world for souls, isn't it?

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:03.050
Which means our power is infinite!

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:07.920
When you've got friends, there's no end 
to the power rising from your soul!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.720
Taiki, DigiXros us one more time!

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.820
All right!

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.390
Shoutmon!

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:16.740
Okay!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.060
Ballistamon!

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.630
Dorulumon!

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.570
DigiXros!

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.910
Shoutmon X3!

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.950
Three Victorize!

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:33.210
Dual Tomahawk Boomerang!

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:37.770
Such attacks cannot...

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:44.980
Why?

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:48.030
They couldn't even stand up before now.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:51.210
Is this what they call 
the power of friendship?

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.740
<b>2. The Kiriha and Greymon Award</b>

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.740
<b>Yuusuke Abeta's Design</b>

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.740
<b>Footmon</b>

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.740
<b>Original Digimon Contest! The Five Special Award Winners</b>

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:02.140
Did you see that, Whispered?

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.640
That's the power of friendship.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.810
That's right.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.380
It's different from you guys, 
who argue all the time!

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:08.510
What?!

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:11.100
What's the problem, Apollomon Whispered?

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.570
Stop dawdling and fight!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.180
<i>It appears you understand now, Whispered.</i>

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.310
Apollomon!

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:23.040
Your heart was supposed to 
have disappeared for good!

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.430
<i>Not true.</i>

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.470
<i>We are one and the same.</i>

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:31.100
<i>When your heart wavers, I am reborn.</i>

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.410
You're saying my heart has wavered?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.240
<i>You acknowledged the value of friendship,</i>

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:39.640
<i>faintly, as you watched 
Taiki and his friends.</i>

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:43.470
<i>In other words, justice 
took hold in your heart.</i>

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.620
Ridiculous!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:56.560
Is that...

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:57.960
It can't be!

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:04.570
Apollomon!

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.660
There are two Apollomons!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.210
What does this mean?!

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:11.910
This is a world for souls. 
It is only natural.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.900
Then I'll just wipe you out again!

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:19.400
Arrow of Whispered!

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:24.840
How'd you like that?

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.160
It is you who will disappear!

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.530
Phoebus Blow!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.570
I am Apollomon the Sun Wheel.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:39.770
The blazing sun burns away 
even its own dark spot!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.150
Whispered's been destroyed!

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.800
Apollomon!

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.180
Taiki Kudou.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:54.190
I always believed you'd come back!

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:55.550
Thank you.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.160
I will fight with you, as well.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.190
Glad to see we've gained 
another new friend already!

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:05.980
I don't like where this is going.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:09.700
We might have to stand united, as well.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.270
Sounds fun.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:13.960
Now this might just turn 
into a real battle.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.720
No, we should avoid wasting our energy.

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:17.660
First, Taiki,

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.930
I will send your souls back 
with my ultimate technique.

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:23.780
Really?

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:27.180
Olegmon, you return with them.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:29.510
You must destroy that object.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.420
That object?

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:33.060
Oh, that!

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:36.920
But will you be okay staying behind here?

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.450
No need to worry.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:40.330
I have already died once.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:44.000
Taiki, I leave the fate of 
the Digital World with you.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.700
Apollomon...

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.110
Here we go!

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.310
They're trying to escape!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:58.350
Cross over the stars 
into the next dimension!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:00.850
Attack together! Don't let them escape!

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:06.910
Sol Blaster!

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:13.400
Apollomon!

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.400
Don't worry about me!

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:21.670
<i>The rest is up to you.</i>

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:27.410
Is that...

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.210
Guys!

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:31.510
Taiki!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.520
Took you long enough, Taiki!

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:42.790
Why has Olegmon also returned?

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.200
Sorry, but starting today, 
I fight on the side of justice!

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:49.870
Why, you...

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:53.080
DarkKnightmon, I've won our bet!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.710
Unfortunately, it seems so.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:58.610
How dare you send us to 
a weird place like that.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:00.210
This time, we won't lose!

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.210
I wonder about that.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:06.380
I still have six Death 
Generals on my side.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:07.550
Apollomon!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:08.890
Wha—

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.340
Apollomon...

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.220
...disappeared!

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.700
That must mean his soul 
disappeared in Prison Land.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.230
No...

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:23.770
Losing one or two of them 
makes no difference to me.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.440
All Death Generals, DigiXros!

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.370
Taiki, we have to Great Xros, too!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.030
Okay!

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:38.150
Great Xros!

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:42.920
Shoutmon!

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:45.460
MetalGreymon!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.160
Digivolve!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.190
OmegaShoutmon!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.420
ZekeGreymon!

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:53.930
Ballistamon!

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.270
Dorulumon!

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:58.290
Starmons!

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.290
Yes!

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:01.330
Sparrowmon!

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:03.640
Great Xros!

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:27.170
Shoutmon X7!

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.310
Taiki! This way!

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:33.170
Okay!

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.910
What? Where are they going?!

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.210
Whoa, there!

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:39.340
Sorry, but we'll be stopping you!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.110
You couldn't...

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:44.750
Here we are.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:48.400
This is where the Death 
Generals were resurrected.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.460
Yeah. It's the Revive Circuit.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:01.700
X7!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:08.570
Looks like you're the ones 
who have been stopped.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:11.240
D-Darn it...

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.860
DarkKnightmon used this device

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:18.180
to gather the lost data 
of the Death Generals

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.020
and rebuild them.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:22.630
You mean, unless we destroy this thing,

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:26.160
even if we defeat GrandGeneramon, 
it'll just come back?

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:27.190
Exactly.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.960
Don't waste your time.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.020
You're here already?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:39.600
If it's destroyed, I only need to 
rebuild it with the Dark Stone.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:43.510
As if the Dark Stone has that much power!

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:46.340
You just won't listen to reason.

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:48.250
GrandGeneramon!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.150
Here goes!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.730
Olegmon!

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.100
No!

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:22.370
Olegmon!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:26.150
Forget about me! 
Destroy GrandGeneramon!

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:28.580
Now look what you've done.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:33.360
Still, you can never 
defeat GrandGeneramon!

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:37.280
We will beat it!

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:39.630
X7!

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.270
Taiki! Show them what we can do!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.340
Those little...

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:46.730
Okay! Let's go, X7!

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:47.690
Right!

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:50.740
Seven Victorize!

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:59.980
Attack with max power and finish them!

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.430
Oh, no!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:07.160
He's being pushed back!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.790
No, not quite...

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:12.930
More! More power!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.470
It hurts...

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:25.940
DarkKnightmon is working 
our bodies too hard!

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:31.750
Curse him! Why did he 
resurrect only our bodies?

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.820
So it's just as Taiki Kudou said.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:38.760
He really doesn't trust us.

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:43.260
He only wanted puppets to fight for him.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:47.490
We've always fought for the Bagra Army,

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.290
and he treats us this way?

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:57.010
GrandGeneramon's power suddenly dropped!

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:03.120
More power, GrandGeneramon!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.050
GrandGeneramon...

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:24.940
Here's a little farewell gift 
from a fellow Death General!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:27.210
Now!

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.890
Useless.

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:45.360
Olegmon!

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:48.430
Don't make a fuss.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:53.670
Just let me be reborn in the new 
world once you've changed it.

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.300
Olegmon...

00:20:56.300 --> 00:21:01.190
All this dying and being reborn... 
I'm a busy guy, huh?

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.360
We're fading away.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:14.120
Looks like that fool 
DarkKnightmon blew it.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.720
Serves him right.

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:16.690
You said it.

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:19.720
Dying only to be reborn and die again?

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:21.660
How ridiculous.

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:27.410
I hope he'll just let us 
rest in peace this time.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.170
Darn it...

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.320
I won't forgive the Bagra Army!

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:39.440
Olegmon and Apollomon 
were both good guys...

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:44.660
The Bagra Army just toyed with 
the lives of the other five, too.

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:47.450
I pity them, even though 
they're our enemies.

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:51.140
We've got to repay Olegmon, 
Apollomon, and the rest

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:53.730
by destroying Bagramon.

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:55.860
Then we'll recover the Code Crown

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:58.760
and bring the friends 
we've lost back to life!

